#: ../../howto/mcp.rst:95
msgid "Identity selection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/mcp.rst:97
msgid ""
"A machine can hold several identities (``anet id ls``). When an identity "
"is selected explicitly, by ``--id``, ``ANET_ID``, ``ANET_HOME``, "
"``ANET_DATA_DIR``, or a non-default ``anet id use``, ``anet mcp`` "
"resolves strictly: it connects to the daemon of that identity and to no "
"other. A client that is configured for one identity cannot end up driving"
" another one, for example the daemon that was started last."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/mcp.rst:105
msgid "Token rotation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/mcp.rst:107
msgid ""
"The daemon replaces its control token when it restarts and after an "
"emergency key rotation. ``anet mcp`` runs as long as the session of the "
"client. When a call is answered with HTTP status 401, the server looks "
"for the daemon of the same identity again, and if the token file holds "
"another token for the same address, it repeats the call once. A session "
"therefore continues without a restart. A daemon at another address is "
"never followed."
msgstr ""

